<article class="env-lemma" id="09S1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09S1">Lemma <span data-tag="09S1">76.44.9</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $i : Z \to Y$ and $j : Y \to X$ be immersions of algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume $j$ is locally of finite presentation and that the sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to i^*\mathcal{C}_{Y/X} \to \mathcal{C}_{Z/X} \to \mathcal{C}_{Z/Y} \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> of Lemma <a href="/tag/06BD" data-tag="06BD">76.5.6</a> is exact and locally split. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $j \circ i$ is a quasi-regular immersion, so is $i$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $j \circ i$ is a $H_1$-regular immersion, so is $i$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If both $j$ and $j \circ i$ are Koszul-regular immersions, so is $i$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from the case of schemes, see Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/068Z" data-tag="068Z">31.22.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>